      "body": "## Pull Request\n\nDiscussion: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/16337\n\n## Description\n\nFixes https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16334\n\n### Problem\nWrapping an async stream return annotation (e.g. `AsyncIterator[T]`, `AsyncIterable[T]`, or `AsyncGenerator[T, None]`) in `typing.Annotated` causes route registration to raise `FastAPIError: Invalid args for response field!` at application startup:\n\n```python\n@app.get(\"/stream\")\nasync def stream() -> Annotated[AsyncIterator[Item], \"metadata\"]:\n    yield Item(name=\"foo\")\n```\n\nThis occurs because `get_stream_item_type()` in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` checks whether `get_origin(annotation)` is in `_STREAM_ORIGINS`. Because the outermost origin of `Annotated[...]` is `Annotated`, `get_stream_item_type` returns `None`. FastAPI then erroneously falls back to treating the entire streaming iterator annotation as a single HTTP response model, which Pydantic cannot serialize as a field.\n\n### Solution\nUnwrap `Annotated` layers in `get_stream_item_type` before evaluating against `_STREAM_ORIGINS`:\n\n```python\ndef get_stream_item_type(annotation: Any) -> Any | None:\n    while get_origin(annotation) is Annotated:\n        type_args = get_args(annotation)\n        if not type_args:\n            break\n        annotation = type_args[0]\n    origin = get_origin(annotation)\n    if origin is not None and origin in _STREAM_ORIGINS:\n        type_args = get_args(annotation)\n        if type_args:\n            return type_args[0]\n        return Any\n    return None\n```\n\nThis restores complete parity between unwrapped `AsyncIterator[T]` and `Annotated[AsyncIterator[T], ...]`:\n- Routes register and run successfully.\n- Yielded stream items are validated against the extracted item type `T`.\n- OpenAPI schema generation correctly emits `itemSchema` for both `application/jsonl` and `text/event-stream` (SSE).\n\n### Tests\nAdded comprehensive test coverage in `tests/test_stream_annotated.py`:\n- `test_get_stream_item_type_unwraps_annotated`: Unit tests verifying `get_stream_item_type` unwrap behavior with single and nested `Annotated` types, sync/async iterators, and non-stream types.\n- `test_stream_annotated_jsonl`: End-to-end JSON Lines streaming with `Annotated[AsyncIterator[Item], \"metadata\"]`.\n- `test_stream_nested_annotated_jsonl`: Nested `Annotated` wrappers.\n- `test_stream_annotated_async_generator`: `AsyncGenerator`.\n- `test_stream_annotated_sync`: Synchronous `Iterator`.\n- `test_stream_annotated_sse`: Server-Sent Events with `EventSourceResponse`.\n- `test_router_stream_annotated`: Streaming route included through `APIRouter`.\n- `test_stream_annotated_openapi_schema`: Verifying generated OpenAPI `itemSchema` for JSONL and SSE endpoints.\n\nAll 8 new tests fail on `master` with `FastAPIError` and pass cleanly with this fix. The existing stream and SSE test suites (67 tests) pass without regression, and all `prek` pre-commit hooks pass.\n\n## AI Disclaimer\n\nPrompt: Diagnose issue #16334 / discussion #16337 in FastAPI regarding Annotated stream return annotations, implement the fix in get_stream_item_type, add comprehensive tests, and ensure all tests and linters pass.\nModel: Gemini 3.8 Flash\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] This PR links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\n- [x] I added tests for the change.\n- [x] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\n- [x] Coverage stays at 100%.\n- [x] The documentation explains the change if needed.\n",
